# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Anthropic API key. Read only in server code, never shipped to the browser.
# Use a key from a dedicated Console workspace with a monthly spend limit set.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Postgres. Neon: use the *pooled* connection string (host contains "-pooler").
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require

# Signs the session cookie. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
# Rotating this immediately logs out every device.
AUTH_SECRET=

# Only used by the one-time migration to accounts (npm run migrate:accounts).
# Once every account exists, delete this line — logins go through
# email + password, and a stale shared secret is a liability.
# APP_PASSPHRASE=

# Her IANA timezone. Day-level dates (workouts, weigh-ins, meals) are computed
# in this zone. Vercel functions run UTC, so leaving this unset means evening
# activity is recorded against the following day. e.g. America/Edmonton
APP_TIMEZONE=UTC

# Google sign-in. Optional — without these, only email + password works.
# Create an OAuth client at console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services →
# Credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application, and register these redirect
# URIs (both, so local and production work):
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/google/callback
#   https://<your-app>.vercel.app/api/auth/google/callback
# Access stays invite-only: signing in with Google only works for an address
# already created with `npm run user -- invite`.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Instacart Developer Platform. With a key, the shopping list gains a "Send to
# Instacart" button and the coach can turn the week's list into a cart —
# Costco and most other grocers in Canada deliver through Instacart. Without
# it the list still works; only that button and tool are unavailable.
# Apply at docs.instacart.com/developer_platform_api — keys start in the
# development sandbox, so set INSTACART_ENV=development until approved.
# INSTACART_API_KEY=
# INSTACART_ENV=production

# Public origin of the deployment, for links back here from a third party
# (Instacart's "back to Coach"). Vercel sets VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL
# automatically, so this is only needed elsewhere.
# APP_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app

# Hard daily spend ceiling, in millionths of a dollar. 500000 = $0.50/day.
# When exceeded, chat pauses until tomorrow; every other screen keeps working.
# DAILY_COST_LIMIT_MICROS=500000

# Other guard rails (defaults shown).
# MAX_CHAT_PER_DAY=250
# MAX_CHAT_PER_MINUTE=8
# MAX_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS_PER_HOUR=10
# MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS=4000

# Two models, split by job. Conversation is frequent and simple; plan and meal
# generation is rare, structured, and where quality actually shows.
# If you change either, update PRICING/PLANNER_PRICING in lib/agent/model.ts
# or the spend cap computes against the wrong prices.
# COACH_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
# PLANNER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
